SUMMARY: 
DESCRIPTION:All Things Open RTP Meetup\nWe'll host our first post-ATO 2026
  meetup on Tuesday evening\, November 10!\n\nThe topic is one we're extrem
 ely interested in and one we get asked about all the time - "**Becoming a 
 More Effective Open Source Contributor Using AI Tooling**". Anyone attendi
 ng should learn a lot!\n\n**Start Time:**\n\n* Doors open at 6:00 pm for n
 etworking\, food and beverages\, and (free) swag\n* Live programming begin
 s at 6:30 pm sharp\n\n**Location:**\nWake Technical Community College - RT
 P Campus\n10908 Chapel Hill Rd.\nMorrisville\, NC 27560\n*\\*We'll be in t
 he auditorium\, which is located in building RT1\, room 162. Enter through
  the side entrance - we'll be there to guide you along.*\n\n**Cost:** FREE
 \, as always\n\n**Speaker:** Brad Topol\, IBM\n\n**Talk Title:** Becoming 
 a More Effective Open Source Contributor Using AI Tooling\n\n**Talk Abstra
 ct:**\nTraditionally\, learning a new open source project and becoming an 
 influential open source contributor was a daunting and painful task that t
 ook several months or years to accomplish. It also relied on spending lots
  of time interacting with project maintainers and exploring GitHub commit 
 histories to understand an open source code base. AI based agentic Integra
 ted Development Environments are having a dramatic impact on what were his
 torically the best practices for becoming an influential open source contr
 ibutor. In this talk\, we cover several case studies where we have explore
 d the use of the AI tools on a variety of popular open source projects and
  evaluate the efficacy of the AI tools. We then provide best practices and
  illustrate how to use these tools effectively. We also describe what pitf
 alls to avoid to ensure that while leveraging these tools\, new open sourc
 e developers are seen as responsible citizens that are making meaningful c
 ontributions as opposed to being seen as non-productive project participan
 ts that are generating “AI Slop” and overwhelming the open source proj
 ect with unnecessary overheads.\n\n**Made Possible By Randstad Digital pow
 ered by Torc**\nThis meetup is in partnership with and made possible by th
 e team at [Randstad Digital powered by Torc](https://www.torc.dev/communit
 y-ato?utm_source=atonewsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=atopartnershi
 p).\n\nRandstad Digital powered by Torc is a global community for technolo
 gy professionals looking to grow their careers\, meet good people\, build 
 new skills\, and stay connected to opportunities along the way.\n\n* [Chec
 k out the website here](https://www.torc.dev/community-ato?utm_source=aton
 ewsletter&utm_medium=email&utm_campaign=atopartnership)\n* [Discord](http:
 //torc.dev/discord)\n* [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/company/torcdot
 dev/)\n* Social handle (all platforms) - @torcdotdev\n* Community Email - 
 [[community@torc.dev](mailto:community@torc.dev)]([mailto:community@torc.d
 ev](http://mailto:community@torc.dev)"[mailto:community@torc.dev](http://m
 ailto:community@torc.dev)")\n* Primary contact - Taylor\, VP of Global Com
 munity\n* Additional team contact - Briana\, Head of Global Operations\n\n
 **RSVP required**\n\\*This is a free event. However\, an RSVP is required.
  Seating is limited\, so RSVP's will be capped as we fill up. Please move 
 quickly and RSVP to save your spot if interested. When you RSVP you will b
 e added to our mailing list to receive future event updates. You can unsub
 scribe at any time.\n\n**Questions?** Contact us at [info@allthingsopen.or
 g.](http://info@allthingsopen.org./)
